"""HSG Advanced — Module 13: hsga-numth2 (Number Theory II).

Fast modular inverse via binary exponentiation, binomial coefficients
mod a prime with factorial tables, prefix sums of Euler's totient, and
a two-congruence CRT checkpoint. Wrong solutions: linear-walk inverses
(timeout), per-query Pascal binomials (timeout), phi recomputed per
query (timeout), and a checkpoint W that reads only the second
congruence (behavioral).

Conventions: zero literal backslashes. Test input AND want use real
newlines via T(); C++ bodies via cpp() turning {{NL}} into \n escapes.
"""
